{"chunk_id": "a50c0865feb8", "text": "As Rama prepares to leave Ayodhya for his fourteen\u2011year exile, the palace is overwhelmed with grief. The minister Sumantra announces Rama\u2019s arrival to the devastated King Dasharatha, who is already crushed by the consequences of Kaikeyi\u2019s demand. When Rama, Sita, and Lakshmana enter, the king rushes toward his son but collapses unconscious from sorrow while the palace women wail in despair. Revived, Dasharatha pleads with Rama to defy the command and seize the throne instead. Rama refuses, insisting that truth and obedience to his father\u2019s word are greater than kingship, pleasure, or even life itself. The king finally blesses him with a heavy heart, recognizing that Rama\u2019s unwavering commitment to dharma cannot be changed. The scene highlights the epic\u2019s central moral conflict between parental love, royal duty, and absolute devotion to truth.\nRama meets his grief-stricken father Dasharatha, refuses the throne, and insists on honoring the exile decree despite the king\u2019s desperate pleas.\nThemes: filial duty, truth and vows, royal grief, exile decision, dharma over power", "vector": [0.012989968061447144, -0.019170187413692474, -0.025059333071112633, 0.0024131962563842535, -0.018709884956479073, 0.01785697415471077, -0.0197252556681633, -0.009828781709074974, -0.024747952818870544, -0.010011549107730389, 0.015758544206619263, 0.014499484561383724, 0.0005914530484005809, 0.01781635917723179, -0.01789758913218975, -0.007628813851624727, 0.04462213069200516, -0.013125350698828697, 0.028565743938088417, -0.006126066204160452, 0.012800431810319424, -0.016841605305671692, -0.007777734659612179, 0.006938362028449774, -0.02229752577841282, 0.007249742280691862, 0.025424866005778313, -0.03641793876886368, 0.027062997221946716, -0.017802821472287178, -0.008278650231659412, -0.018533887341618538, 0.005621765740215778, -0.019292030483484268, -0.031192168593406677, 0.013578882440924644, -0.008502031676471233